<?xml version="1.0"?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

<!-- Shallow-water wreck manipulation, modeled on GVK-Derelicts' own dereliction pattern
     (GVK-Universal-Dereliction.sbc / GVK-Other-Recovery-Manipulation-COALITION): guns knocked
     down, cargo cleared and replaced with a much smaller loot pool than the live ships (reuses the
     existing WW2-Loot-Small tier rather than inventing a new one), no RivalAI combat wiring since
     these never fight back.

     2026-09-13: [UseRandomNameGenerator:true] + [RandomGridNamePrefix:Wreck - ] added to each
     wreck's Manipulation below, so the grid displays as "Wreck - Gabbiano" etc. MES only supports
     a PREFIX here (ManipulationProfile.cs has RandomGridNamePrefix but no suffix equivalent) - a
     true "Gabbiano - Wreck" suffix isn't achievable via SpawnGroup/Manipulation tags without either
     editing the shared prefab's baked-in DisplayName (which would also rename the live ship) or a
     C# mod, so the user chose the prefix as the closest available option. (Superseded 2026-09-20, see below: the pattern route does allow a suffix.)

     2026-09-14: reworked per user feedback on the first live La Malouine test spawn - only one gun
     showed any visible damage, and every gun looked fully built (100% BuildPercent, only hidden
     IntegrityPercent was low, per the note in the previous version of this comment). Two changes:

     1) Corrected/expanded the [Blocks:] lists below. Re-checked every prefab with a stricter
        xsi:type-to-SubtypeName pairing script (matching each <MyObjectBuilder_CubeBlock xsi:type=...>
        to the very next <SubtypeName>, rather than eyeballing grep context) and found several real
        guns missing from the original lists - notably BoforSingleRemodel (present on nearly every
        hull) and Type96Single/TTMK15Triple on some destroyers. Deliberately excluded ammo/prop
        blocks that also use ConveyorSorter but aren't guns themselves: 139mmHEShell, 13mmAmmoBox,
        20mmDrum, 40mmClip, M2BrowningAmmoBox (all ammo storage props), LargeBlockConveyorSorter
        (plain conveyor sorter, not a weapon at all), and TTMK15Torpedo (the stored torpedo prop, not
        the TTMK15Triple launcher/tube itself) - all Le Triomphant-only except LargeBlockConveyorSorter,
        which also appears on Comandante Margottini.

     2026-09-14, second pass: briefly added TTMK15Torpedo to the Destroyer-Guns list, per the user
     calling it a real gun/launcher rather than an ammo prop - then removed again per the user's own
     follow-up. Net result: still excluded, same as the original call.

     2) [Chance:100]/[MinBuildPercentage:100]/[MaxBuildPercentage:100] (uniform, invisible-looking
        damage) initially replaced with [Chance:70] + [MinBuildPercentage:10]-[MaxBuildPercentage:60]
        (~30% of guns left fully intact). Per the user, that wasn't the intent - no gun should be
        intact - so this is now [Chance:100] + [MinBuildPercentage:15]-[MaxBuildPercentage:20]: every
        matched gun gets touched, and always ends up heavily wrecked (low but still randomized, per
        "a range of derelict effects"). IntegrityPercent stays at 1-15 (already low, and ProcessBlock
        always clamps Integrity <= Build anyway, so it never reads as inconsistent with the Build
        roll).

     2026-09-20: Spica wreck added and reuses the Destroyer wreck manipulation, so 100mmSingleMain and
     OerlikonDual (Spica's guns, both checked in its prefab) were added to WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Destroyer-Guns.
     Spica's 100mmMLE1931Shell and 20mmDrum are ammo props and LargeBlockConveyorSorter is a plain
     sorter, so those stay excluded like the other hulls.

     2026-09-20, later: guns read below 15 percent in-game because IntegrityPercent was still 1-15 (the
     HUD shows integrity, not build). Switched to [UseSeparatePercentages:false] with
     [MinPercentage:15]/[MaxPercentage:20], so ProcessBlock gives each gun the SAME random value for
     both build and integrity (DerelictionProfile.cs). Inference from the user's report, not yet
     confirmed in-game.

     2026-09-20: gun build range raised from 5-15 to 15-20 (5-15 looked too stripped). Wreck naming
     reworked: the old prefix-only route (else-if branch in PrefabManipulation.cs) cannot touch
     antennas, so each wreck now uses the pattern route: [RandomGridNamePattern:Wreck] makes the
     new name "Wreck" and it becomes the HUD text of the first antenna and first beacon (matched
     by a name containing Antenna or Beacon, HUD text instead of block name). The grid name is
     prefix + "Wreck" with the bare word DefaultGridName swapped for the original name (per
     RandomNameGenerator.ProcessGridname), so wrecks now read "Gabbiano - Wreck", the suffix
     wording originally asked for. Not yet confirmed in-game. The Golo antenna has no CustomName in
     the prefab, so MES falls back to the block definition name (Compact Antenna), which should
     still contain Antenna.

     Also added [SkinRandomBlocks:true] to each wreck's Manipulation, reskinning most of the grid to
     a mix of Heavy_Rust_Armor and Rusty_Armor (both confirmed as real vanilla skin SubtypeIds in
     Content/Data/AssetModifiers/ArmorModifiers.sbc). SkinRandomBlocks picks uniformly at random
     from [SkinRandomBlocksTextures:] per block (CosmeticEffects.cs RandomBlockSkinning) - there's no
     weighting field, so the requested 60/40 split is faked by listing Heavy_Rust_Armor three times
     and Rusty_Armor twice in a 5-entry list (3-in-5 = 60%, 2-in-5 = 40%). Coverage range
     (Min/MaxPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:95/100) wasn't specified by the user - chosen to reskin
     nearly the whole grid rather than a small patch, since "change the skin on blocks" read as a
     whole-hull weathering pass, not a partial one; retune if that reads as too uniform in-game.
     Applied identically to all three wreck tiers (Golo/Corvette/Destroyer) per the user's ask that
     these manipulations apply to all of these wrecks. -->

	<EntityComponents>

		<!-- Golo wreck guns: Type96Single AA guns, 5InchSingleMain deck gun, and the WeaponCore
		     turret controller driving them. Re-checked 2026-09-14 with the stricter pairing script -
		     this list was already complete, no additions needed. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Golo-Guns</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[MES Dereliction]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/Type96Single]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/5InchSingleMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_TurretControlBlock/LargeTurretControlBlock]
			[MatchOnlyTypeId:false]
			[Chance:100]
			[UseSeparatePercentages:false]
			[MinPercentage:15]
			[MaxPercentage:20]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<!-- Wrapper Manipulation: clears the Golo's normal cargo, applies the dereliction above,
		     reduces the loot pool to the Small tier, and reskins most of the grid to rust. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Manipulation-Golo-Wreck</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[MES Manipulation]
			[ManipulationChance:100]

			[ClearGridInventories:true]

			[UseGridDereliction:true]
			[DerelictionProfiles:WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Golo-Guns]

			[UseLootProfiles:true]
			[LootProfiles:WW2-Loot-Small]

			[UseRandomNameGenerator:true]
			[RandomGridNamePattern:Wreck]
			[RandomGridNamePrefix:DefaultGridName - ]
			[ReplaceAntennaNameWithRandomizedName:Antenna]
			[ReplaceAntennaHudTextInsteadOfName:true]
			[ReplaceBeaconNameWithRandomizedName:Beacon]
			[ReplaceBeaconHudTextInsteadOfName:true]

			[SkinRandomBlocks:true]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Rusty_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Rusty_Armor]
			[MinPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:95]
			[MaxPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:100]

			[GridsAreEditable:true]
			[GridsAreDestructable:true]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<!-- Corvette wrecks (Gabbiano/La Malouine) gun list, corrected 2026-09-14: added
		     Type96Single (Gabbiano) and BoforSingleRemodel (La Malouine), both missed by the
		     original grep-based pass. BlockStates.ProcessDereliction just iterates the grid's own
		     blocks and checks each one against this list, so a subtype absent from a given hull is
		     a harmless no-op - safe to share one profile across both hulls. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Corvette-Guns</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[MES Dereliction]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/13mmTwinMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/100mmSingleMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/Type96Single]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/5InchSingleMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/BoforSingleRemodel]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/FAM2BrowningTurret]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_TurretControlBlock/LargeTurretControlBlock]
			[MatchOnlyTypeId:false]
			[Chance:100]
			[UseSeparatePercentages:false]
			[MinPercentage:15]
			[MaxPercentage:20]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Manipulation-Corvette-Wreck</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[MES Manipulation]
			[ManipulationChance:100]

			[ClearGridInventories:true]

			[UseGridDereliction:true]
			[DerelictionProfiles:WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Corvette-Guns]

			[UseLootProfiles:true]
			[LootProfiles:WW2-Loot-Small]

			[UseRandomNameGenerator:true]
			[RandomGridNamePattern:Wreck]
			[RandomGridNamePrefix:DefaultGridName - ]
			[ReplaceAntennaNameWithRandomizedName:Antenna]
			[ReplaceAntennaHudTextInsteadOfName:true]
			[ReplaceBeaconNameWithRandomizedName:Beacon]
			[ReplaceBeaconHudTextInsteadOfName:true]

			[SkinRandomBlocks:true]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Rusty_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Rusty_Armor]
			[MinPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:95]
			[MaxPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:100]

			[GridsAreEditable:true]
			[GridsAreDestructable:true]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<!-- Destroyer wrecks (Francesco Crispi, Comandante Margottini, Bougainville, Le Triomphant)
		     gun list, corrected 2026-09-14: added BoforSingleRemodel, TTMK15Triple, and Type96Single,
		     all missed by the original grep-based pass (present on at least one of the four hulls).
		     Deliberately excludes 139mmHEShell/13mmAmmoBox/20mmDrum/40mmClip/M2BrowningAmmoBox/
		     LargeBlockConveyorSorter (ammo-storage props and a plain conveyor sorter, not guns) and
		     TTMK15Torpedo (the stored torpedo, not the TTMK15Triple launcher - briefly added then
		     removed again same day, see the file-level comment above). -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Destroyer-Guns</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[MES Dereliction]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/100mmTwinMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/138mmMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/OerlikonMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/FAM2BrowningTurret]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/13mmTwinMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/BoforSingleRemodel]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/TTMK15Triple]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/Type96Single]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/100mmSingleMain]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_ConveyorSorter/OerlikonDual]
			[Blocks:MyObjectBuilder_TurretControlBlock/LargeTurretControlBlock]
			[MatchOnlyTypeId:false]
			[Chance:100]
			[UseSeparatePercentages:false]
			[MinPercentage:15]
			[MaxPercentage:20]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Manipulation-Destroyer-Wreck</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[MES Manipulation]
			[ManipulationChance:100]

			[ClearGridInventories:true]

			[UseGridDereliction:true]
			[DerelictionProfiles:WW2-Wreck-Dereliction-Destroyer-Guns]

			[UseLootProfiles:true]
			[LootProfiles:WW2-Loot-Small]

			[UseRandomNameGenerator:true]
			[RandomGridNamePattern:Wreck]
			[RandomGridNamePrefix:DefaultGridName - ]
			[ReplaceAntennaNameWithRandomizedName:Antenna]
			[ReplaceAntennaHudTextInsteadOfName:true]
			[ReplaceBeaconNameWithRandomizedName:Beacon]
			[ReplaceBeaconHudTextInsteadOfName:true]

			[SkinRandomBlocks:true]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Heavy_Rust_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Rusty_Armor]
			[SkinRandomBlocksTextures:Rusty_Armor]
			[MinPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:95]
			[MaxPercentageSkinRandomBlocks:100]

			[GridsAreEditable:true]
			[GridsAreDestructable:true]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

	</EntityComponents>
</Definitions>
